  "id": "py-split-remainder",
  "integration_required": false,
  "intent": "Splitting an expense loses cents. `split_evenly(100, 3)` in `tally/money.py` returns `[33, 33, 33]`, which adds up to 99, so the balances for a ledger with such an expense no longer sum to zero.\n\nExpected behaviour of `split_evenly(total, n)`:\n\n- The shares always add up to `total`, and no two shares differ by more than one cent.\n- The earlier shares (participants are in the order given) take the extra cents: `split_evenly(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`.\n- A negative total (a refund) mirrors the positive case: `split_evenly(-100, 3) == [-34, -33, -33]`.\n- `n` must be positive; otherwise `split_evenly` raises `ValueError`.\n\n`checks/split-repro.sh` reproduces the problem. The tests run with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -q`.\n",
  "lease_epoch": 1,
  "max_attempts": 3,
  "state": "done",
  "workflow": {
   "name": "bug-fix",
   "version": 1
  }
 }
